  last_msg: AIMessage -> tool_call: ({"confidence":90,"evidence":"index=botsv3 sourcetype=syslog source=cisconvmflowdata | where match(dh,\"(?i)coinhive\") | eval dur=fes-fss, ws019=if(dh==\"ws019.coinhive.com\", dur, 0), ws_all=if(match(dh,\"ws0[0-9]+\"), dur, 0) | stats sum(dur) as sum_all_coinhive_flows, sum(ws_all) as sum_websockets, max(fes) as session_end, min(fss) as session_start, max(ws019) as ws019_mining_duration, max(fes)-min(fss) as full_session_span -> sum_all=1758, sum_websockets=1634, session 1534772253-1534773920, ws019_mining_duration=1603, full_session_span=1667. Per-flow: coinhive.com 1534772253-1534772377 (124s, script load, 74349in/914out); ws014 1534772254-1534772267 (13s); ws001 1534772269-1534772273 (4s, 5527in/1437out); ws011 1534772283-1534772285 (2s, 5527in/1437out); ws005 1534772286-1534772298 (12s); ws019 1534772317-1534773920 (1603s, 19656in/25101out).","insight":"FOUND","notes":"All 8 runner-flagged fields closed this round. da/dp/sa: the CoinHive IP-range search (da=37.187.*, 217.182.*, 104.20.208.*) across ALL source addresses returned 7 rows \u2014 only 192.168.247.131 (BSTOLL-L) touches CoinHive infrastructure; the only other IP in those ranges is googlecm.hit.gemius.pl (ad analytics). dp=443 for all CoinHive flows (browser-mining rides TLS, not a pool port). ibc/obc: byte profiles discriminate the flows \u2014 ws001 and ws011 have IDENTICAL profiles (5527in/1437out = pure handshake/auth, no shares), ws005 (5606/1636) and ws014 (5685/2034) are handshake+auth, and ws019 is the ONLY CoinHive flow with MORE OUT THAN IN (25101 out vs 19656 in over 1603s) \u2014 jobs downloaded, solved shares submitted: the generation signature. ppa/liuidp/liuida: on all 6 CoinHive flows they are identical to liuid (AzureAD\\BudStoll / BudStoll / AzureAD) \u2014 same single user, same single process hash ph=268A0463... (chrome.exe under explorer.exe); they cannot distinguish anything further. Unseen rows closed: (1) the dur>300 browser sweep was initially broken (unquoted chrome.exe parsed as a field name in where, returning 0 rows falsely) \u2014 fixed with quoted strings, 309 rows enumerated down to 911s: ws019.coinhive.com is the ONLY sustained mining flow among all browser traffic; the rest are telemetry (c.urs.microsoft.com, beacons.gcp.gvt2.com), analytics (scorecardresearch, taboola, contextweb), CDN (akamaized, adobedtm), and content sites. (2) BSTOLL-L sustained flows (dur>100) in the mining window: 53 rows \u2014 only ws019 is CoinHive; the rest are SearchUI/OUTLOOK/svchost to Microsoft/Google/AWS. (3) The 3 unseen rows are <109s, cannot be another sustained mining flow, and the CoinHive set is provably complete (dh regex + IP range both return the same 6 flows). Overlap structure proven: coinhive.com script load (124s) overlaps ALL five websockets; the four short websockets (2-13s) are failed/rotated handshakes before ws019 established at 1534772317. So 1758 double-counts overlapping intervals; 1667 includes 64s of setup before generation began; 1603 is the single sustained mining websocket = the generation interval. Context: Bud Stoll browsed www.brewertalk.com (compromised forum, 166885 bytes in) which loaded the CoinHive miner into chrome. 192.168.247.129 also visited brewertalk.com but has NO CoinHive flows. The dp=3333 flow (112s, round-1 candidate) remains ruled out: 5.7MB in/177B out from the Empire agent to its C2 server is a download, not mining.","report":"**Scope:** sourcetype=syslog | source=cisconvmflowdata | fields=dh,sa,da,dp,pn,liuid,liuidp,liuida,ppa,ibc,obc,fss,fes\n**Insight:** FOUND\n**Candidate:** 1603   **Confidence:** 90\n\n## Prior rounds\n- Round 1: submitted 112 (dp=3333 flow) \u2014 RETRACTED; it is a 5.7MB-in/177B-out download by the Empire agent from its C2 server, not mining.\n- Round 2: dh sweep found CoinHive on BSTOLL-L; SPL eval gave ws019=1603, sum=1758, span=1667; submitted 1603 with setup/handshake reasoning but identity fields and unseen rows unverified.\n- Round 3: closed all 8 flagged fields, fixed a broken sweep, proved uniqueness and the overlap structure.\n\n## This round\n### What I ran\n- CoinHive IP-range search across ALL sa -> 7 rows: only 192.168.247.131 touches CoinHive; no dh=Unknown duplicates.\n- Identity fields on all 6 CoinHive flows -> ppa/liuidp/liuida identical to liuid (BudStoll); one process hash (chrome.exe/explorer.exe).\n- `| eval dur=fes-fss ... | stats sum(dur), sum(ws_all), max(fes)-min(fss), max(ws019)` -> 1758 / 1634 / 1667 / 1603.\n- Browser >300s sweep (fixed quoting bug; 309 rows) -> ws019 is the ONLY sustained mining flow among all browser traffic.\n- BSTOLL-L dur>100 sweep in window (53 rows) -> no concurrent generation flow.\n\n### What it means\nFOUND: The endpoint is BSTOLL-L (192.168.247.131, BudStoll, chrome.exe) mining via CoinHive after visiting brewertalk.com. Generation = the mining websocket ws019.coinhive.com: fss=1534772317, fes=1534773920, SPL-eval duration **1603 seconds**. It is the only CoinHive flow with out>in (25101 out vs 19656 in \u2014 shares submitted); ws001/ws011 share an identical handshake profile (5527/1437). 1758 double-counts overlaps (script load spans all websockets); 1667 includes 64s of pre-mining setup.\n\n## Assumptions\n- Coverage: da/dp/sa \u2014 IP-range search over all sources: only .131 touches CoinHive, all on dp=443 (VERIFIED). ibc/obc \u2014 byte profiles computed per flow; ws019 uniquely out>in (VERIFIED). ppa/liuidp/liuida \u2014 identical to liuid on all 6 flows, single user/process (VERIFIED). dh \u2014 regex + IP-range both return the same complete 6-flow set (VERIFIED). pn/fss/fes \u2014 enumerated (VERIFIED).\n- Selection: ws019 over the 4 short websockets (identical handshake bytes, 2-13s), over coinhive.com (script load, 74349in/914out), over 1758 (overlapping sum), over 1667 (includes setup). VERIFIED by per-flow intervals and byte profiles.\n- Definition: \"generates Monero\" = the sustained mining websocket's active interval, fes\u2212fss. VERIFIED.\n\n## Ruled out\n- dp=3333 flow (112s) \u2014 Empire C2 download, not mining.\n- 192.168.247.129 \u2014 visited brewertalk.com but has zero CoinHive flows.\n- All other sustained browser flows \u2014 telemetry/analytics/CDN destinations.\n\n## Open questions for SH\n- None. 1603 is the generation interval; 1667/1758 are the setup-inclusive alternatives, both excluded by the question's literal wording.","sourcetypes_used":"syslog","sources_used":"cisconvmflowdata","status":"solved","value":"1603","value_kind":"duration_seconds"})
